-- MoveMyBags -- player-facing strings.
--
-- Every string the player can see lives here, keyed by its English text, so a
-- translation is a table of English -> translated and nothing in the addon's
-- logic changes. A key with no translation falls back to the English, so a
-- partial translation is still usable and a new string never shows as nil.
--
-- Chat output uses |cffffff78...|r for the commands it mentions; keep those
-- markers in a translation, they are what makes the command stand out.

local _, ns = ...

local L = setmetatable({}, {
    __index = function(_, key)
        return key
    end,
})
ns.L = L

local locale = (GetLocale and GetLocale()) or "enUS"

-- English is the key, so enUS needs no entries. The list below is every
-- string the addon uses, for translators to copy. Keep it complete: a string
-- missing here is a string nobody knows needs translating.
--
--   "MoveMyBags"
--   "Lock bag windows"
--   "Stops bag windows being dragged. Saved positions still apply, and the resets still work."
--   "Connect windows while dragging"
--   "A window you drag clicks flush against its neighbours and slides around them instead of over them. Off, it goes exactly where the cursor puts it."
--   "Close the hole a moved bag leaves"
--   "The column closes up around a bag you drag out of it, and re-opens when you put it back. Off, Blizzard's column is left exactly as it is."
--   "Keep the window you are using in front"
--   "Each window sits on its own layer, and the one you pick up or click comes to the front. Off, the windows are drawn in whatever order the client has them."
--   "Separate arrangements at the bank and at a merchant"
--   "Blizzard lays the bags out differently beside the bank, and both the bank and a merchant open every bag. On, each place remembers its own arrangement once you move a bag there, and follows your usual one until you do. Off, one arrangement is used everywhere."
--   "Show the bag windows in Edit Mode"
--   "A placeholder for each bag appears in Edit Mode, at the bag's position, and can be dragged like any other part of the UI. Off, Edit Mode leaves the bags alone."
--   "Follow Edit Mode layouts"
--   "When an Edit Mode layout becomes active, including at login, a MoveMyBags layout with the same name is loaded. Save one with /movemybags save <name>. Off, Edit Mode layouts and bag arrangements are unrelated."
--   "Backpack"
--   "Bag %d"
--   "Reagent bag"
--   "Keyring"
--   "Combined bags"
--   "Put back"
--   "This character keeps its own arrangement"
--   "Starts from a copy of the account-wide arrangement, and from then on this character's bags are arranged on their own. Off, the account-wide arrangement is used; this character's is kept for next time."
--   "Reset positions"
--   "Put every bag window back"
--   "Every window returns to Blizzard's own slot, in every context and both bag modes. Shift-right-click a window to put just that one back."
--   "Drag a window by its frame to move it, or Shift-drag its title bar. Shift-right-click a window to put it back."
--   "Lock or unlock bag windows"
--   "Left-click: options. Right-click: lock or unlock."
--   "Windows are locked"
--   "Windows are unlocked"
--   "all bag positions reset."
--   "all bag positions reset, in every context."
--   "the %s arrangement is forgotten; it follows your usual one again."
--   "give the layout a name of up to %d characters: %s"
--   "layout '%s' saved."
--   "layout '%s' loaded."
--   "layout '%s' deleted."
--   "no layout called '%s'. %s lists them."
--   "no saved layouts. %s saves the current arrangement under a name."
--   "saved layouts: %s"
--   "bags are already locked."
--   "bags are not locked."
--   "bags locked. %s to move them again."
--   "bags unlocked."
--   "drag a bag window by its frame to move it, or Shift-drag its title bar. Shift-right-click a window to put it back. %s puts them all back; %s stops them being dragged; %s opens the options; %s shows what the addon is doing."
--   "%s, %s and %s keep arrangements by name; %s lists them. The bank and a merchant each remember their own arrangement once you move a bag there."
--   "this client's bag layout is not one this addon can re-stack, so the column is left as Blizzard draws it. Dragging still works."
--   "hit an error. %s shows it; please report it. %s"
--   "standing down for this session after %d errors. The bag windows are Blizzard's again until you %s."
--   "status failed: %s"
--   "options are not available on this client."

if locale == "enUS" then
    return
end

-- Translations live on CurseForge, not in this file: the project's
-- localization page is where translators work, and the packager replaces each
-- @localization@ line below with that locale's translated strings at release
-- time, as `L["English"] = "translated"` lines. A string nobody has translated
-- yet is left out (handle-unlocalized="ignore") and falls back to English.
-- From a source checkout the lines stay comments and every block is empty, so
-- the addon runs in English.
--
-- Until the repository variable CF_LOCALIZATION is "true", the release and
-- alpha builds skip CurseForge and bake the drafts in docs/localization/ into
-- these lines instead (tools/localization.lua bake).
--
-- The strings above reach CurseForge through .github/workflows/localization.yml,
-- and docs/localization/ holds the first drafts it seeded. Adding a string
-- means adding it to the list above; tests/suites/locales.lua fails if one is
-- used and not listed.
--
-- esMX takes esES's translations, then anything translated for esMX itself.

-- luacheck: push ignore 542
